config SOC_ESP32C3_POWER_LATCH
    bool "Drive the power latch high at reset"
    default $(dt_has_nodelabel,power_latch)
    depends on SOC_ESP32C3
    help
      Drive the pin of the board's power_latch node high as the first
      thing the early init does, before there are devices: a board that
      powers itself from the battery through it stays on once the power
      button is released. The device that owns the pin keeps it high.

config SOC_ESP32C3_POWER_OFF
    bool "Power off by dropping the power latch"
    default y
    depends on SOC_ESP32C3_POWER_LATCH && $(dt_has_nodelabel,charger)
    select SOC_HAS_POWER_OFF
    help
      Power off by driving the power latch low, which disconnects the
      battery once the power button is up. The input of the charger
      node tells USB power, which keeps the board on regardless: then
      the chip resets instead, as without this.

config SOC_ESP32C3_FLASH_CLOCK_DIV
    int "Flash clock divider"
    range 1 4
    default 4
    depends on SOC_ESP32C3
    help
      The flash's clock, and so the speed of code and data run in place,
      is the 80 MHz of the PLL divided by this: 4 is the 20 MHz the boot
      leaves, 2 is 40 MHz and 1 is 80 MHz. Applies with the CPU on the
      PLL only. The early init reads the image's first 16 KiB back at the
      new clock and returns to the old one if it reads differently.
